te problem. The initial prototypes are currently being tested in the field, demonstrating their potential. This innovation seeks to tackle the increasing challenge of waste generated by conventional wind turbine blades, with plans for larger models aimed at commercial projects on the horizon.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/german-startup-voodin-replaced-fibreglass-with-laminated-veneer-lumber-in-19-3-metre-turbine-blades-its-new-eu-backed-factory-targets-fully-recyclable-blades-at-commercial-scale/articleshow/133229906.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/german-startup-voodin-replaced-fibreglass-with-laminated-veneer-lumber-in-19-3-metre-turbine-blades-its-new-eu-backed-factory-targets-fully-recyclable-blades-at-commercial-scale/articleshow/133229906.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T11:08:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133230043,imgsize-103047.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado mom gets her son ‘arrested’ after he refuses to take a first-day-of-school photo]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133230154.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-mom-gets-her-son-arrested-by-police-after-he-refuses-to-take-a-first-day-of-school-photo-with-officer-handcuffing-him-in-hilarious-prank/articleshow/133230154.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-mom-gets-her-son-arrested-by-police-after-he-refuses-to-take-a-first-day-of-school-photo-with-officer-handcuffing-him-in-hilarious-prank/articleshow/133230154.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T11:23:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133230299,imgsize-1185920.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After 14 years, Massachusetts dam removal begins to restore 7 miles of stream]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133216344.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-conservationists-began-working-to-remove-an-obsolete-massachusetts-dam-14-years-later-demolition-started-to-reconnect-7-miles-of-stream-and-restore-6-acres-of-wetland/articleshow/133216344.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2012-conservationists-began-working-to-remove-an-obsolete-massachusetts-dam-14-years-later-demolition-started-to-reconnect-7-miles-of-stream-and-restore-6-acres-of-wetland/articleshow/133216344.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T10:42:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133216452,imgsize-141309.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Six generations return to Lake Winnipesaukee for a century-old tradition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133157996.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/six-generations-have-vacationed-at-new-hampshires-lake-winnipesaukee-one-family-still-spends-thousands-each-summer-to-keep-the-tradition-alive/articleshow/133157996.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/six-generations-have-vacationed-at-new-hampshires-lake-winnipesaukee-one-family-still-spends-thousands-each-summer-to-keep-the-tradition-alive/articleshow/133157996.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T10:42:20+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133158064,imgsize-148815.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Owens Reframes Kirk Assassination: Owens says grief fuels spiritual mission; video blends faith and audience engagement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133226534.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Candace Owens has opened up about how her feelings changed following Charlie Kirk’s assassination. She said she has moved beyond the initial trauma and no longer feels haunted, instead believing Kirk is spiritually “fighting alongside” her. Owens connected her optimism to her belief that truth will prevail and said she feels Charlie is still with them. She also encouraged viewers to support her show by purchasing merchandise.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/candace-owens-says-she-feels-charlie-kirk-is-fighting-alongside-her-as-she-opens-up-about-his-assassination/articleshow/133226534.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/candace-owens-says-she-feels-charlie-kirk-is-fighting-alongside-her-as-she-opens-up-about-his-assassination/articleshow/133226534.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T05:32:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133226541,imgsize-97869.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amazon AI Opt-Out Backlash: Twitch auto-enables training on streams; creators must change privacy settings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133226553.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Twitch is facing criticism over a new setting that allows Amazon to use streamer content for generative AI training by default. Streamers can opt out through their privacy settings. Users questioned why the option was not turned off unless creators agreed. Twitch said it is not training GenAI models itself, but the setting covers Amazon’s AI model training.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/twitch-faces-furious-streamer-backlash-as-amazon-ai-training-opt-out-appears-enabled-by-default/articleshow/133226553.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/twitch-faces-furious-streamer-backlash-as-amazon-ai-training-opt-out-appears-enabled-by-default/articleshow/133226553.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T05:19:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133226554,imgsize-53592.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Old Graduation Clip Resurfaces: Clavicular’s virtual ceremony goes viral; fans see quieter past]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133226558.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A resurfaced video from Clavicular’s COVID-era middle school graduation has gone viral, giving fans a wholesome glimpse of the streamer before his rise to internet fame. The footage shows his name being announced during a virtual ceremony while his parents celebrate from home. Now 20, Clavicular has built a large following through IRL streams, looksmaxxing content and controversial online discussions, making the old clip especially surprising for fans.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/claviculars-old-graduation-video-sparks-massive-reaction-as-fans-discover-the-streamers-life-before-fame/articleshow/133226558.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/claviculars-old-graduation-video-sparks-massive-reaction-as-fans-discover-the-streamers-life-before-fame/articleshow/133226558.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T05:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133226566,imgsize-75950.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Paranormal Creator’s Fatal Crash: Jiang Xiaorou dies after July accident; family urges fans to stop speculation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133226573.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jiang Xiaorou, a 24-year-old Chinese paranormal content creator, died on August 10 after suffering severe injuries in a July 15 traffic accident. Known for challenging superstition, she had more than 1.28 million Douyin followers. Her controversial videos, including one showing her destroying a Guanyin statue, resurfaced after her death. However, there is no evidence linking her accident to supernatural punishment, despite speculation circulating online.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/who-was-jiang-xiaorou-the-haunting-story-of-the-chinese-tiktoker-whose-death-brought-her-most-controversial-video-back/articleshow/133226573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/who-was-jiang-xiaorou-the-haunting-story-of-the-chinese-tiktoker-whose-death-brought-her-most-controversial-video-back/articleshow/133226573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T06:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133226629,imgsize-99309.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote by Karl Popper: 'Those who promise us paradise on earth never produced anything but a hell']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133223683.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Karl Popper highlighted the dangers of striving for a perfect society, warning that such aspirations frequently lead to disastrous outcomes. He pointed out how leaders driven by utopian dreams tend to accumulate excessive power, often resulting in brutality. The French Revolution and several authoritarian regimes serve as stark illustrations of this trend. In the current era, technological advancements and corporate ideologies can echo these same pitfalls.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-karl-popper-those-who-promise-us-paradise-on-earth-never-produced-anything-but-a-hell-and-the-deadly-psychological-flaw-behind-every-political-utopia/articleshow/133223683.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-karl-popper-those-who-promise-us-paradise-on-earth-never-produced-anything-but-a-hell-and-the-deadly-psychological-flaw-behind-every-political-utopia/articleshow/133223683.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T01:50:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133223855,imgsize-877049.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Zeno: 'We have two ears and one mouth, so we should listen more than we say']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133220714.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Zeno of Citium, originally a Phoenician trader, established Stoicism in the heart of ancient Athens. He advocated that true listening is an intentional skill rather than simply a precursor to responding. This timeless philosophy champions the value of understanding prior to action. Contemporary studies validate that active listening boosts trust and mitigates conflict, emphasizing the age-old design of our auditory and vocal apparatus.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-zeno-we-have-two-ears-and-one-mouth-so-we-should-listen-more-than-we-say-and-why-2300-years-of-human-evolution-still-havent-fixed-our-obsession-with-talking/articleshow/133220714.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-zeno-we-have-two-ears-and-one-mouth-so-we-should-listen-more-than-we-say-and-why-2300-years-of-human-evolution-still-havent-fixed-our-obsession-with-talking/articleshow/133220714.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T00:50:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133220916,imgsize-1201504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by CT Fletcher: "Everything is impossible, until someone crazy enough comes along and…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133220879.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-ct-fletcher-everything-is-impossible-until-someone-crazy-enough-comes-along-and-a-lesson-in-persistence-and-unconventional-thinking/articleshow/133220879.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-ct-fletcher-everything-is-impossible-until-someone-crazy-enough-comes-along-and-a-lesson-in-persistence-and-unconventional-thinking/articleshow/133220879.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T23:42:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133221776,imgsize-80888.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1962, New Jersey took a family's property; they challenged the price and were awarded $350,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133220258.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Exploring vintage postcards reveals a fascinating glimpse into coastal life in early New Jersey. Historian John Joseph Patrick Mulhern recounted his experiences on Sandy Hook, describing the thrilling days of tracking ships and conducting groundbreaking radio experiments. He vividly portrayed the operations of the Navesink lighthouses and the evolving landscape, showcasing the rich maritime heritage and community growth of the time.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1962-new-jersey-took-a-familys-seaside-property-through-eminent-domain-for-a-new-park-they-challenged-the-price-and-were-awarded-350000/articleshow/133220258.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1962-new-jersey-took-a-familys-seaside-property-through-eminent-domain-for-a-new-park-they-challenged-the-price-and-were-awarded-350000/articleshow/133220258.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-13T23:14:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133220422,imgsize-1000991.cms"/></item></channel></rss>